<article class="env-remark" id="8B1A3F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8B1A3F">Remark <span data-tag="8B1A3F">2.4.2.2</span>.</a> Let $F: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ be a functor between (ordinary) categories. The induced map of simplicial sets $\Nerve (F): \Nerve (\calC ) \rightarrow \Nerve (\calC ')$ of simplicial sets is automatically an inner fibration; it is Cartesian if and only if $F$ is a <em>fibration</em> of categories in the sense of Grothendieck. </p>
